  "slug": "biological-brain-types-006a",
  "summary": "Repository-scale pretraining and independent chromatographic checks are now being applied to improve confidence in metabolite annotation from tandem MS.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is improving confidence in compound annotation from tandem mass spectra and chromatographic data. UltraMS is a dual-polarity foundation model pretrained on over 160 million tandem mass spectra, aimed at molecular identification and structure elucidation. LipidRT adds a chromatographic check: it uses retention time coherence to validate and expand lipid annotations in untargeted reversed-phase LC-MS lipidomics. What is new is the combination of large-scale spectral pretraining in UltraMS with retention time validation in LipidRT. MSGFLEX, a proteomics and metaproteomics pipeline, and gutenTAG, a MALDI-IHC processing and quality control tool, address different analytical problems and are not annotation methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
